-- GAME ----------------------------------------------------------------------
  Title       Arkanoid
  Publisher   Imagine, 1987
  Version     1.0

-- YOU NEED ------------------------------------------------------------------
  Your own copy of the original game, saved beside this patch:

  File        Arkanoid (1987)(Imagine).z80
  MD5         1f0faef52a701cfc9434e2745ccb7fc2

  The patch carries none of the game's code. It only works with that exact
  dump, under that name or any other: anything else is refused, with a
  message naming the file it wants.

-- WHAT IT DOES --------------------------------------------------------------
  Moving figures become Next hardware sprites, so they keep their own colours
  and no longer take on the scenery's (colour clash). Game logic is unchanged.

  Colours     Default (the game's own) plus: Arcade, chosen on the menu, off
              by default.
  Enhanced    Arcade-style colours: the Vaus with red ends, aqua bands and a
              silver body; a white ball; each capsule in its arcade colour
              with its letter cut out (S orange, L red, E blue, D aqua, B
              pink, C green, P grey); orange to red cones, red, green and blue
              molecules, aqua cubes, green pyramids, a fiery explosion and
              orange and red pieces from Doh. A painted set, colourist not
              named.

  Note        Keys: any key past the title, the scores and the story; Z left,
              M right (bottom rows), A to G or ENTER to launch and fire; a
              Kempston joystick works. The bat, balls, capsules, aliens and
              laser are Next sprites over their own pixels, so they keep their
              own colours instead of a brick's or the background's; the
              bricks, walls, score panel and Doh's face stay as the game draws
              them. The original's clash is small (the ball and capsules
              passing over bricks, Doh's bullets over his face); Arcade
              colours are the reason to choose this patch.

-- MENU ----------------------------------------------------------------------
   1  Infinite lives

  Checked against this release's code: 33702 is the DEC A after the life count
  is loaded; a NOP there keeps the count. Not played.

