-- TESTING -------------------------------------------------------------------
  Tested      NexClash differential verification against six recordings; run
              from its menu in OverSpec with Arcade colours and the cheat on;
              Tang FPGA board: default and Arcade colours load and play.
              Colours approved by the owner, 2026-11-21. Not played by a
              person.

  Replay      IDENTICAL on 6 machine-played recordings, 65,443 frames (rounds
              1-11 without a cheat; rounds 9, 17 and 25 and Doh's round 33 by
              the game's own round counter; the attract demo), default and
              Arcade colours alike: at every hook original and patched code
              from the same state (every register but R, all memory), every
              figure's sprite pixels against the game's own XOR pixels (25.6
              million compared), and every pattern row sent against the colour
              model (4.9 million rows); unit tests on every plot kind,
              graphics and position pass for both sets; 8 of 8 negative
              controls detected, and 3 more for the colour route (jump left
              off, a data page empty, the ball's page empty)

  Emulator    OverSpec, from the patch menu: Arcade colours and Infinite lives
              on, title, story and round 1 reached with the arcade Vaus

  Coverage    Machine-played recordings only: rounds 1-11 with all 7 capsules,
              rounds 9, 17, 25 and 33 entered by the round counter; rounds
              12-16, 19-24 and 27-32 not reached (same engine, level data);
              beating Doh, the ending and high score entry not reached

  Hardware    Tang Nano 20K FPGA build of the Next, with DivMMC automap on and
              124 sprites left visible by a previous program: default and
              Arcade colours load, play (the floating bus wait the game
              depends on works), no crash

  Nothing here claims a result on real hardware unless the line above says so.

-- HOW TO USE ----------------------------------------------------------------
  Put this .nxc and the game file in the same folder on the Next's card and
  choose the .nxc in the Browser. See README.txt.
